.TH ENGINE_TOP 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
engine_top \- The scene currently on top of the stack, or NULL when empty
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqengine.h\(dq
.BI "Scene * engine_top(Engine *e);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The scene currently on top of the stack, or NULL when empty. Useful to guard against pushing a scene twice: if (engine_top(e) != shop_scene()) engine_push(e, shop_scene()). Queued changes are not reflected until they apply.
.PP
This is a static inline function; it is defined in the header.
.SH RETURN VALUE
the top Scene pointer or NULL.
.SH MODULE
core (src/engine/core/engine.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR engine_push (3),
.BR Scene (3),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
